# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE (steps/defects.md): User's code reads a1\x through its hidden input a1, a root merge
# result whose admission by name takes the merge result's own Structure as its model (K02c).  u1, a merge copy of
# User, runs with a copy C of the unit as its node (MERGE-PARENT-SITE-OVERRIDE): the model is C's own copy a1' of the
# declaration's instance -- an ordinary Structure read from the copied lexical graph -- and the value is the root's a1,
# the caller's binding first.  The copy takes a1's record with itself to a1': the original a1 is admitted to the
# copied requirement by the same correspondence (lmx_copy_carry_records).  a2, which no copied code reads, is absent
# from C.  Exit 7; 81 if u1 read anything but a1's 1.
Model:
    int: x 1
end: Model
a1: merge: Model
a2: merge: Model
User:
    int: y 0
    y: a1\x
end: User
u1: merge: User
u1
int: ok 7
if: u1\y != 1
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
